Feature: Data Validation and Processing for Purgo Playground Schema

  Background:
    Given the dataset is loaded into the purgo_playground schema
    And the dataset has the following fields: country_cd, product_id, qty_sold, sales_date

  Scenario: Validate Data Format and Integrity
    Given the dataset is loaded
    When the data is processed for validation
    Then the country_cd field must be a valid country code of two uppercase letters
    And the product_id must follow the format 'P' followed by four digits
    And the qty_sold must be a positive integer
    And the sales_date should be in the format YYYY-MM-DD

  Scenario Outline: Calculate Total Quantity Sold Per Product
    Given the dataset is filtered by country_cd "<country_cd>"
    When the total quantity sold per product_id is calculated
    Then the total quantity for product_id "<product_id>" should be "<total_qty>"

    Examples:
      | country_cd | product_id | total_qty |
      | US         | P1001      | 50        |
      | US         | P1002      | 30        |
      | CA         | P1001      | 40        |
      | CA         | P1003      | 25        |

  Scenario Outline: Identify Error for Missing Data
    Given the dataset is processed
    When a row is missing required data
    Then an error message "Missing required data in row <row_number>" should be displayed

    Examples:
      | row_number |
      | 5          |
      | 10         |

  Scenario: Error on Incorrect Date Format
    Given a sales_date of "15-01-2024"
    When data validation is run
    Then an error message "Incorrect date format in sales_date, expected YYYY-MM-DD" should be displayed

  Scenario Outline: Calculate Total Sales for Given Product
    Given the dataset contains sales data
    When the data is processed for total sales
    Then the total sales for product_id "<product_id>" across all countries should be "<total_sales>"

    Examples:
      | product_id | total_sales |
      | P1001      | 150         |
      | P1002      | 103         |
      | P1003      | 70          |
      | P1004      | 75          |

  Scenario: Validate Sales Date Range
    Given the sales_date is present in the dataset
    When the data is processed
    Then sales_date should not be a future date

  Scenario: Error on Negative Quantity Sold
    Given a qty_sold of -10 for product_id "P1004"
    When the data is processed
    Then an error message "Quantity sold must be a positive integer" should be displayed
